{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-10-27 06:00:00', 'title': 'S&P GLOBAL FINDS THAT CLOSING THE MEDIAN WAGE GAP HAS BEEN A NET DISADVANTAGE FOR WOMEN', 'text': 'NEW YORK, OCT. 27, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0S&P GLOBAL (NYSE: SPGI) TODAY RELEASED A FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND RESEARCH REPORT ANALYZING THE GENDER WAGE GAP AND ITS EVOLUTION OVER THE LAST 15 YEARS. THE NEW REPORT, "GLASS FLOORS AND CEILINGS: WHY CLOSING THE MEDIAN WAGE GAP ISN\'T FAIR," FOUND THAT COMPARED TO MEN, WOMEN IN EXECUTIVE ROLES ARE MORE LIKELY TO RECEIVE COMPENSATION IN A COMPRESSED RANGE AROUND THE MEDIAN OF THEIR PEER GROUP (FIGURE 1).'}